<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <div class="hero-subtitle">Department of Linguistics</div>
    <h1>Mentoring Archive</h1>
    <p class="hero-statement">
      A record of the mentored learning experiences that shape our
      students &mdash; research collaborations, conference presentations,
      teaching apprenticeships, editorial internships, study abroad,
      and the everyday conversations that redirect a career.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<main class="main">

  <!-- About the archive -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2>About This Archive</h2>
    <p>
      Mentoring is central to what we do in the Department of Linguistics
      at Brigham Young University. Faculty in TESOL, English Applied
      Linguistics, Editing &amp; Publishing, Linguistic Computing, and
      Linguistics work alongside students on published research,
      conference presentations, applied projects, and community engagement.
      This archive documents that work and its outcomes.
    </p>
    <p>
      The archive serves several purposes. It gives faculty a place to
      record mentoring activities for annual reports and rank-and-status
      reviews. It gives current and prospective students concrete examples
      of what mentored learning looks like in our department. And it lets
      students reflect on how their mentored experiences shaped their
      development along the four
      <a href="https://aims.byu.edu/aims-of-a-byu-education" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Aims of a BYU Education</a>:
      spiritually strengthening, intellectually enlarging,
      character-building, and lifelong learning &amp; service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- The two archives -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2>Two Views of the Same Story</h2>

    <div class="panels">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Faculty Mentoring</h3>
        <p>
          Faculty-authored records of coauthored research, conference
          presentations, teaching assistantships, thesis supervision,
          study abroad programs, curriculum development, and other
          mentoring activities. Each entry includes the students
          involved, the accomplishments, and the mentor's reflection
          on what the experience produced.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="FacultyMentoring/view.html" class="btn btn-primary">Browse faculty entries</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Student Experiences</h3>
        <p>
          Student reflections on transformative mentored experiences,
          organized by the four Aims. Students describe what they
          worked on, who they worked with, and how the experience
          shaped their intellectual, spiritual, character, and
          service-oriented development.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="MentoredStudent/student-view.html" class="btn btn-primary">Browse student reflections</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Contributing -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2>Contribute an Entry</h2>
    <p>
      Faculty and students in the Department of Linguistics are invited to
      contribute to the archive. Submissions go through short Google Forms
      and are reviewed by the department before appearing on the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      Contributors decide what appears publicly. Any submission can be
      marked entirely private, and individual fields can be flagged to
      keep them out of the public view. Students may share their
      reflections anonymously if they prefer.
    </p>

    <div class="panels">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Faculty</h3>
        <p>
          Document a mentoring activity, project, or outcome &mdash; a
          coauthored paper, a conference presentation, a lab
          assistantship, a study abroad program, curriculum work, or an
          office-hour conversation that mattered.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd1W_Q90Q4yzKKRn0lQjG-Sm-dmK_NUo2xRBQOH9zmJE8hldw/viewform" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">Submit faculty entry</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Students</h3>
        <p>
          Share a mentored experience that shaped you &mdash; a research
          project, an internship, a course that changed your direction,
          a conversation with a mentor. Reflect on how it developed you
          across the Aims of a BYU Education.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeywfK4kLT_hr1-ZMiMd0-GcE463EaFKrDcEiaOaeaqdlfjAQ/viewform" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">Submit student experience</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Privacy -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2>A Note on Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The archive is designed to respect the choices of contributors.
      Faculty and students who submit can:
    </p>
    <ul style="font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.7; padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      <li>Mark specific fields as private &mdash; they stay in the
          departmental record but never appear on this site.</li>
      <li>Mark an entire entry as private &mdash; the departmental
          record keeps it, but nothing about it is published.</li>
      <li>(Students) Share their reflection anonymously &mdash; their
          name appears as &ldquo;Anonymous student&rdquo; on the
          public page while the department retains the original for
          its records.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Submissions are reviewed before publication. If you have
      questions, please contact the department office.
    </p>
  </section>

</main>

